{"article_ids": ["f3a4701b135347c8"], "canonical_title": "CIFQA: A Deterministic Tool-Grounded Multi-Agent LLM Framework for Financial Query Answering", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.85, "description": "The paper CIFQA (arXiv:2608.26114v1) presents a new deterministic, tool‑grounded multi‑agent large language model framework designed for calculation‑intensive financial question answering. It targets exact reasoning over structured rates, temporal conditions, numerical formulas, and rule‑based constraints, addressing the tendency of standard LLMs to produce numerically incorrect but plausible answers.", "entities": ["term:cifqa"], "first_seen": "2026-08-28T04:00:00Z", "id": "evt_f3a4701b135347c8", "importance_score": 6.29, "last_updated": "2026-08-28T04:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-ai"]}
{"article_ids": ["5413cacb7968c78f"], "canonical_title": "CARE: Causally-Aligned Reasoning Exploration for Medical Large Language Models", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.78, "description": "Researchers presented CARE (Causally-Aligned Reasoning Exploration), a new approach for training medical LLMs. It targets the scarcity of expert-annotated data by using reinforcement learning while addressing two known problems: autoregressive credit‑assignment failure and gradient‑variance explosion, which can cause models to produce correct answers for the wrong reasons.", "entities": ["term:care"], "first_seen": "2026-08-28T04:00:00Z", "id": "evt_5413cacb7968c78f", "importance_score": 5.64, "last_updated": "2026-08-28T04:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-cl"]}
{"article_ids": ["62284d0edfcb91d9"], "canonical_title": "FedCMAPSS: A Benchmark for Federated Learning in Remaining Useful Life Estimation", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.85, "description": "The authors introduced FedCMAPSS, a benchmark that provides a dataset and evaluation framework specifically for applying federated learning to remaining useful life (RUL) estimation tasks. It addresses the prior absence of a common evaluation platform for FL‑based prognostics models.", "entities": ["term:rul"], "first_seen": "2026-08-28T04:00:00Z", "id": "evt_62284d0edfcb91d9", "importance_score": 5.64, "last_updated": "2026-08-28T04:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-lg"]}
{"article_ids": ["70ee64ba58194281"], "canonical_title": "Why did My Robot Just Change Personality? Prompting Guidelines for a Grounded Robot Persona in LLM-Based HRI", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.78, "description": "The paper presents a new framework for designing prompts used by large language models in social robots and proposes a structured prompt template that consists of eight functional components. The framework aims to address underspecified prompt design that can cause hallucinated capabilities, unclear behavioural boundaries, and misleading robot personas.", "entities": ["term:hri"], "first_seen": "2026-08-28T04:00:00Z", "id": "evt_70ee64ba58194281", "importance_score": 5.64, "last_updated": "2026-08-28T04:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-ai"]}
{"article_ids": ["8146504a8eb67b82"], "canonical_title": "Standalone LLM and a Pre-specified Agentic Pipeline for Explaining ICU Mortality Predictions: a Feasibility Study on the eICU Demo Dataset", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.73, "description": "A feasibility study was conducted using the eICU Demo Dataset to compare two approaches for generating explanations of ICU mortality predictions: a standalone large language model (LLM) and a pre‑specified multi‑step agentic pipeline that separates data interpretation, guideline checking, and final explanation. The study preserves the original comparison between the two methods while evaluating their ability to produce clinically useful narratives.", "entities": ["term:icu"], "first_seen": "2026-08-28T04:00:00Z", "id": "evt_8146504a8eb67b82", "importance_score": 5.39, "last_updated": "2026-08-28T04:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-ai"]}
